{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q016_pdb_1acc_domain_split","answer":"In SCOP 1.75, 1acc chain A was a single whole-chain domain, d1acca_ (sunid 43828), classified in family f.11.1.1 within fold f.11 'Anthrax protective antigen' in class f (membrane and cell surface proteins). In SCOPe 2.08 the chain is split into two domains in different classes: d1acca2 (sunid 238522, A:14-225) in b.179.1.1 'PA14', superfamily b.179.1 'PA14-like', fold b.179 'Anthrax protective antigen N-terminal-like', class b all-beta; and d1acca1 (sunid 238521, A:226-735) in f.60.1.1 'Anthrax protective antigen C-terminal-like', fold f.60, class f. Fold f.11 was retired and the new folds received new sunids (254103 for f.60, 254104 for b.179), so identifiers do not carry over. Both 2.08 domains keep the 'complexed with ca' comment and the Bacillus anthracis species node; the chain maps to UniProt P13423 and its 2.08 sequence-cluster representative is 3tewA, not 1accA.

What it reveals: the N-terminal region, formerly a protein-specific single-member unit, is now recognized as a PA14 module shared at the family level with unrelated proteins; the 2.08 PA14 family also contains a yeast beta-glucosidase PA14 domain protein node (sunid 254417, Kluyveromyces marxianus). Family membership is a homology assertion between these domains even though the full-length proteins have different functions and partner domains. The 1.75 whole-chain definition conflated two segments with separate evolutionary histories, so the old fold f.11 was an artifact of under-splitting. The C-terminal region remains a class f unit but is now its own fold/superfamily/family containing only this protein, so no homology beyond the protein itself is asserted for it in 2.08.

Implications for homology searches: query and template domain-wise, using d1acca2 and d1acca1 separately rather than the whole chain. Hits to the PA14 domain imply homology only to the N-terminal module, not to the C-terminal region, and do not justify transferring the anthrax protein's function to glycosidases or adhesins carrying PA14. Family (b.179.1.1) and superfamily (b.179.1) membership are the evolutionarily strong claims; shared fold alone is not evidence of common ancestry. Relatives of the C-terminal f.60.1.1 domain are not supplied by SCOPe 2.08 and would require external profile or structural evidence. Pin the release, because 1.75-based ASTRAL subsets use d1acca_/f.11 and are not comparable to 2.08 without remapping. Stored hits for representative 3tewA are evidence for that representative, not an official classification of 1acc.","evidence_used":["mcp__scope__get_scop_pdb_entry","mcp__scope__get_scop_chain","mcp__scope__get_scop_domains","mcp__scope__get_scop_node","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1acc","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1acc/chains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1acc/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/1accA","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca1/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca1/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca1/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca2","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca2/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca2/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca2/homology","/api/v1/releases/1.75/sids/d1acca_","/api/v1/releases/1.75/sids/d1acca_/parents","/api/v1/releases/1.75/sids/d1acca_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/1.75/pdb/1acc","/api/v1/releases/1.75/pdb/1acc/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/b.179.1.1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/b.179.1.1/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/f.60.1.1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/f.60.1.1/parents"]}]}
